<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # The Environment and Recycling – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 8th Grade (CEFR: A2.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Environment and Recycling</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> In the Past, People Didn't Recycle as Much as They Do Now.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Analyze informational texts for specific purposes. Reading: Interpret characters' motives in short stories. Phonemic Awareness: Demonstrate knowledge of phonemic awareness by pronouncing the past tense verbs ending "ed."</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can analyze informational texts for specific purposes, such as recycling tips (e.g., "Identify two ways to save water from the text.")<br>Can interpret motives behind actions in short texts about sustainability (e.g., "Why should we recycle?").<br>Can pronounce past tense verbs ending in "ed" (e.g., produces the appropriate sounds /d/, /ɪd/, and /t/ in words like "saved," "wasted," and "watched").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: left; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays two large images side-by-side on the board: one showing a street with a lot of trash and no recycling bins (labeled "In the Past") and another showing a clean street with clear recycling bins (labeled "Today"). Students observe the images silently for 30 seconds. Then, the teacher asks, "What do you see in the 'Past' picture? What do you see 'Today'?" guiding students to use vocabulary like 'waste', 'pollution', 'recycle', 'clean', 'environment'. The teacher encourages students to read the labels for contrasting past and present practices.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher points to the images and says, "In the past, people <b>wasted</b> a lot. They didn't <b>recycle</b> much. Today, people <b>protect</b> the planet more. We <b>saved</b> many resources." The teacher explicitly models the pronunciation of past tense verbs ending in "-ed", focusing on /d/ in 'saved', /ɪd/ in 'wasted', and /t/ in 'watched' (if used in previous examples). The teacher writes the words on the board, underlining the '-ed' ending and indicating the sound.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did people recycle *often* in the past?" (No, they didn't.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What sound does 'saved' end with: /d/, /ɪd/, or /t/?" (/d/)</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Environment and Recycling".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher distributes a short informational text titled "Recycling: Then and Now" (approximately 150-180 words). The text contrasts past practices regarding waste with current recycling efforts and includes tips for saving water. It incorporates target vocabulary (recycle, waste, environment, pollution, energy, landfill, planet, resource, reduce, reuse, clean, save, protect, environmental, important, carefully, often) and grammar (past simple vs. present practices, modal 'should', first conditional).
                <br><i>Example excerpt:</i> "In the past, many families didn't think about recycling; they simply *wasted* materials. Our grandparents often *threw* everything into one bin. This *polluted* the *environment*. Today, we are more *aware* of protecting our *planet*. If we *reduce* our waste, we *will save* natural *resources*. You *should* turn off the tap carefully when brushing your teeth to *save* water."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Reading: Can analyze informational texts for specific purposes. Reading: Can interpret motives behind actions in short texts.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the text individually.
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Reading:</b> Students read the text once to understand the main idea. "What is the text mainly about?" (a. How people recycled in the past. b. How recycling has changed over time. c. How to save water.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read the text again to answer True or False questions.
                        <ol style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">In the past, people often reused old items. (False, according to example excerpt)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Today, people are more careful about protecting the environment. (True)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Turning off the tap saves water. (True)</li>
                        </ol>
                    </li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Past simple vs. present practices ("In the past, people didn't recycle that much." "Today people are more aware..."), First conditional ("If we waste water, there will be less..."), Modal 'should' ("You should turn off the tap...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> recycle, waste, environment, pollution, energy, landfill, planet, resource, reduce, reuse, clean, save, protect, environmental, important, carefully, often.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Practice the pronunciation of past tense "-ed" endings: /d/ (saved), /ɪd/ (wasted), /t/ (watched).</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ol style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice (Gap-fill):</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences from the text, but with key vocabulary and past tense verbs removed. They read the sentences and fill in the blanks using a word bank. (e.g., "In the past, people often ___ (waste) many materials." "We ___ (should) protect our planet.") The teacher monitors and helps.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Sentence Completion:</b> Students work individually to complete sentences based on the text and their understanding of past vs. present practices. (e.g., "In the past, people didn't recycle, so..." "If we waste too much water,..." "To protect the environment, you should...") The teacher guides them to use the first conditional and modal 'should'.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation & Peer Check:</b> In pairs, students take turns reading aloud their completed sentences from activity 1 and 2. Their partner listens carefully, checking for correct use of vocabulary and especially the pronunciation of the "-ed" endings in past tense verbs. The teacher circulates, offering immediate feedback and re-modeling sounds as needed (e.g., "Listen: /wɑːtʃt/ not /wɑːtʃɪd/").</li>
                </ol></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Environment and Recycling".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Reading Analysis and Problem Solving.
                Students are divided into small groups (3-4 students). Each group receives a short fictional "case study" paragraph (around 80-100 words) describing an environmental issue in a local community, highlighting a change in practice from past to present. For example, "In the past, Riverdale community *dumped* all trash near the river. Now, the community *wants* to be cleaner, but many people still *don't separate* their trash. The river *is getting* very *polluted*."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group reads their case study carefully.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The group identifies the environmental problem and compares past practices (what happened) with current challenges (what is happening now). They underline or highlight relevant sentences.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The group then brainstorms and writes down 2-3 solutions, using phrases like "If we [action], there will be [effect]." and "We should [action] to [protect/save/reduce]." They must use at least three target vocabulary words and two past tense verbs (from the text) in their summary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group prepares to briefly present their identified problem and proposed solutions to the class, focusing on summarizing what they read and analyzed.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group work and quick check of written responses to a short reading task.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students receive a new, short paragraph (approx. 50 words) about a community initiating a new recycling program.
                <br><i>Example:</i> "Last month, the community of Green Valley *started* a new recycling program. Before this, many residents *discarded* all waste. Now, they *have learned* to separate plastic and paper. If everyone *participates*, the *landfill* will be smaller, and the *environment* will be cleaner. People *should* support this important change."
                <br>Students read the paragraph and answer the following questions on an exit ticket:
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Identify one way Green Valley changed its waste practices.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What is the main motive for the community to recycle?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Underline two past tense verbs and indicate their '-ed' pronunciation sound (/d/, /ɪd/, or /t/).</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and accuracy in identifying information from the text (reading for specific purposes).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to interpret motives (e.g., cleaner environment).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Demonstrated knowledge of "-ed" phonemic awareness in identifying and articulating the sounds.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of target vocabulary (observed during group work).</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most interesting fact you read today about recycling?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"On a scale of 1-5, how well can I understand informational texts about the environment?"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">6-8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of today's reading activity did you find most challenging? How did you overcome it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can the information we read today help you make better choices for the environment?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this reading lesson? (e.g., student engagement with the texts, their ability to identify key information, pronunciation practice).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students struggling with text comprehension or pronunciation? (e.g., provide a glossary, more simplified texts, one-on-one pronunciation drills).</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> The next lesson will focus on Speaking & Interaction. Students will use the knowledge gained from reading about past and present environmental practices and recycling tips to discuss and propose solutions orally in groups, drawing directly from the texts analyzed today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>